{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Howzit, come in, have a seat. What's been going on?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Shame, doctor, I had to drag him here. He has asthma, and he's been wheezy since that cold. He just shrugs when I ask.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): Ja.",
  "[SEG0004] person_1 (DOCTOR): Tell me how it's actually been feeling.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (PATIENT): Tight.",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (DOCTOR): Tight in the chest. When did that start?",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (PATIENT): Monday.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Monday, ja. I was going to say a week, but no — the wheeze is four days. The cold itself was the week before.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): Is that cold still on you, or has it moved on?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (CAREGIVER): The nose is better now. He was blocked and sniffing all of last week.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): And a cough, has there been one?",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (PATIENT): Ja.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Dry cough, worse at night. He was hacking around two this morning.",
  "[SEG0014] person_1 (DOCTOR): Bringing up any phlegm, or is it staying dry?",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (PATIENT): Dry.",
  "[SEG0016] person_1 (DOCTOR): Have you felt feverish, hot or shivery?",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (CAREGIVER): I felt his forehead, no temperature. He is tired, though, properly washed out.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Is it only that tight feeling, or are you short of breath too?",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (PATIENT): Walking.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Even from the car he was puffing. The robot by the parking was out, so we walked an extra bit and he had to stop.",
  "[SEG0022] person_1 (DOCTOR): Eish, those robots. Sorry you waited as well, the room was hectic.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Ag, it's fine. I had a book.",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (DOCTOR): You've got pumps at the flat, hey? What do you actually reach for when it starts?",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (PATIENT): Blue.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (CAREGIVER): He says blue, but he mixes them up. It gets tight and he grabs the brown one, and I have to swap it.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): Easy done. The blue one is the reliever, salbutamol, for the wheeze right then. The brown one is the preventer, every day, even on a good day. Which have you mostly used this week?",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (PATIENT): Blue.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Mostly the blue, once it's actually in his hand. He's been living on it.",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (DOCTOR): How often in a day, do you think?",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Maybe five, six times a day. More if he takes the stairs.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (DOCTOR): And each time, how many puffs is that?",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (CAREGIVER): He was doing one puff... no, sorry, two puffs of the salbutamol, for the wheeze. I watched him this morning.",
  "[SEG0034] person_1 (DOCTOR): Okay. The brown one, beclomethasone — are you still taking it?",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (CAREGIVER): He stopped. Hundred micrograms, two puffs in the morning and two at night. I nearly said he'd been off it two weeks, but it ran out and he never fetched another, so it's about a month.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (DOCTOR): Before it ran out, was that twice a day really happening?",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (CAREGIVER): I can't honestly say. Some mornings the counter hadn't budged. I'm not sure he took it the way it was prescribed.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any asthma tablets on top of the pumps?",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Montelukast. I always muddle the strength — the five milligram... no, his is the ten milligram one, at night. He stopped that as well, said it did nothing.",
  "[SEG0041] person_3 (PATIENT): Nothing.",
  "[SEG0042] person_1 (DOCTOR): Did anyone give you an antibiotic for the cold?",
  "[SEG0043] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Amoxicillin, from the clinic. He never took a single capsule. The bottle is still full in the cupboard.",
  "[SEG0044] person_1 (DOCTOR): Then that one doesn't count. Anything else, even a chemist bottle?",
  "[SEG0045] person_2 (CAREGIVER): A cough mixture, the purple one. He took it once, went drowsy, and left it. I don't know the name.",
  "[SEG0046] person_1 (DOCTOR): We'll leave the nameless one. Besides the cough, was anything else wrecking the night?",
  "[SEG0047] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Loadshedding till all hours, and he was on his phone. Ag, not very medical, sorry.",
  "[SEG0048] person_1 (DOCTOR): No, I asked. Jacket up a bit, let me listen. Breathe easy, don't push it.",
  "[SEG0049] person_3 (PATIENT): Okay.",
  "[SEG0050] person_1 (DOCTOR): Wheeze both sides, a bit louder on the left. No crackles. Sister got your oxygen at ninety-six percent when you came in.",
  "[SEG0051] person_1 (DOCTOR): The peak flow she wrote as two hundred and eighty — ag, wrong line. It's three hundred and forty litres a minute.",
  "[SEG0052] person_2 (CAREGIVER): He's around five hundred when he's well. Hates that little plastic tube.",
  "[SEG0053] person_1 (DOCTOR): So this is a real dip for you. Any pain in the chest?",
  "[SEG0054] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0055] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any blood when you cough?",
  "[SEG0056] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0057] person_2 (CAREGIVER): His appetite's been off as well. Sunday braai, he ate a roll and then went to lie down. Not like him.",
  "[SEG0058] person_1 (DOCTOR): Eating less, alright. How's sleep been?",
  "[SEG0059] person_3 (PATIENT): Bad.",
  "[SEG0060] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Bad because of the cough. He falls asleep, then the hacking wakes him.",
  "[SEG0061] person_1 (DOCTOR): Are you at varsity, or working?",
  "[SEG0062] person_3 (PATIENT): College.",
  "[SEG0063] person_2 (CAREGIVER): First year. Stays with me in the Rondebosch flat in term — I'm the carer, not his mom. His parents are in Gqeberha.",
  "[SEG0064] person_1 (DOCTOR): Getting to class, or home these last days?",
  "[SEG0065] person_3 (PATIENT): Home.",
  "[SEG0066] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Missed two days. Moody about a test on Thursday, but that's just varsity.",
  "[SEG0067] person_1 (DOCTOR): Shame, man. What I'm hearing is an asthma flare after the cold, worse because the preventer lapsed and the blue pump's been carrying everything.",
  "[SEG0068] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'll add a steroid course. Prednisone forty milligrams... ag, no, thirty milligrams, once a day, by mouth, for five days, and take the first one today with a bit of food.",
  "[SEG0069] person_1 (DOCTOR): Keep using the salbutamol, two puffs when you're tight. Please restart the brown beclomethasone too, two puffs morning and night, every day, not only when you wheeze.",
  "[SEG0070] person_2 (CAREGIVER): I'll stick it next to his toothbrush, otherwise it just sits.",
  "[SEG0071] person_1 (DOCTOR): If you're still needing the blue one more than four times a day after a couple of days, tell me. We might do a chest x-ray if this doesn't settle, but not today. Let's see you in two weeks. If the breathing gets harder before then, come straight back.",
  "[SEG0072] person_3 (PATIENT): Sharp.",
  "[SEG0073] person_2 (CAREGIVER): We'll fetch the prednisone at Dis-Chem. Thanks, hey."
 ],
